WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:03.569
Bladesmiths,
welcome to the forge,

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:06.072
where, typically,
we'd start you at your anvils.

00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:08.775
There's no point today.
There are no tools.

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.042
Instead, your tools

00:00:10.175 --> 00:00:12.678
are behind our very own
<i> Forged In Fire...</i>

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.580
[suspense music]

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:15.882
steel grate.

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:18.284
Or "grate wall." Ha ha.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:20.119
Grate wall? Get it? G-R-A-T-E.

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:21.587
-Grate wall? Okay.
-[crickets chirp]

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.755
[all chuckle]

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:26.692
Your job is to free your tools

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.360
from this steel grate

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:32.331
<i> and make a blade using nothing
 but this grate wall.</i>

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:34.634
<i> Some of this is mild,
 some of this is high-carbon.</i>

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.870
<i> It's up to your skill set
 to determine what's what</i>

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.639
<i> and forge your blade.</i>

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:40.940
<i> The length of your blade</i>

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.975
<i> must be between
 12 and 14 inches</i>

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:44.276
<i> with a through tang.</i>

00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:47.413
Good luck, bladesmiths,
your three hours starts... now.

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:49.582
[Bobby]<i> We all go straight
 to the grate wall</i>

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:50.650
and we work as a team.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.985
[buzzing]

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.587
I'm pouring sparks down
onto poor Dallas.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:00.193
[Wil] These guys
just yanked this entry way

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.261
right out of our grate wall.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.630
And now they gotta harvest
all those little pieces.

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:05.865
[action theme music]

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.435
[Wil] Look at Will,
he's just moving down his grate.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:11.804
Very methodically
just knocking off

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.207
those small pieces of rod.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.944
You got enough?

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.311
[Justin]
<i> These tiny little pin stock.</i>

00:01:19.411 --> 00:01:20.613
<i> You're not gonna stack it
 all up</i>

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:23.115
<i> and weld it together
 into a little billet.</i>

00:01:23.148 --> 00:01:24.750
<i> So you gotta do
 canister Damascus.</i>

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.552
<i> I'm skipping the White Out.</i>

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.455
I'm just gonna forge-weld
that canister

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:29.522
right to the billet,

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.091
because
I can grind it off later.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.993
[Bobby]<i> The only canisters left
 are canoe canisters</i>

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.195
<i> and I've never done
 a canoe before.</i>

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.231
<i> I'm thinking, okay,
 if this is gonna be the same</i>

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:39.365
<i> as a regular canister,</i>

00:01:39.431 --> 00:01:41.201
then I've got a lot more
welding to do.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:44.937
I decided to use White Out
and let it dry

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:46.506
<i> so the hard metal steel</i>

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:48.908
and the powder
doesn't adhere to that.

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:51.410 line:0%
[David] Bobby's got White Out
in his can.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.213 line:0%
He took time to dry it.
That's smart work.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.149 line:0%
They're really gonna try
and wow us with the pattern.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.551
Removing that can
is gonna give us a better look.

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:01.487
[Bobby]
<i> Weld in a topple in there,</i>

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:04.190
weld in a work stick on it
and then the fire.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.525
My welding skills suck.

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:09.562
<i> I am just gopping this stuff
 all around there</i>

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.865
<i> because I don't wanna have
 any open seam</i>

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.099
<i> and it starts
 shooting out sparks</i>

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.734
<i> and I gotta start over again.</i>

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.672
My first squeeze on the press
feels really good.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.841
It's solid. I can feel it go
all the way down.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.342
[Doug] Bobby.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:26.078
The color when he brought
that out was a bright yellow.

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:27.747
It got really massive
with the heat.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.715
That thing's about to fall off.

00:02:29.815 --> 00:02:33.552
I get my canister up to temp
and I start mashing it down.

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:37.556
I lose my handle at the press
because I'm a crappy welder.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.292
[Wil] That's about
to pop off there, right there.

00:02:40.325 --> 00:02:42.028
What're you gonna do, Justin?

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:44.164
-Weld like that-- There you go.
-There he goes.

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:49.302
[Justin]<i> So I re-weld
 the stick back on.</i>

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.004
-Oh!
-Whoa!

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:53.372
And that falls off again too.

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:55.575
[Bobby]<i> I'm looking around,
 I see these other guys</i>

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:56.308
<i> already got blades.</i>

00:02:56.608 --> 00:02:58.677
I'm thinking I'm behind
the eight ball here.

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:00.212
[banging]

00:03:00.345 --> 00:03:02.782
[Wil] Bobby is the only one
of our smiths

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:05.551
who freed his billet
from the can

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:08.320
so that put him a little bit
behind everybody else.

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:09.555
[David]
If Bobby works it now,

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:12.124
he could actually start
getting ahead of the pack.

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:13.192
He doesn't have to worry

00:03:13.258 --> 00:03:14.927
about grinding any steel
off that blade.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:18.064
[Bobby]<i> Each press pass
 runs really well.</i>

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.333
And each time I gain
a little bit more.

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:21.700
<i> And now I have something</i>

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.670
<i> that's beginning to look more
 like a knife.</i>

00:03:24.703 --> 00:03:26.739
[Will]<i> I used Big Blue
 for the first time.</i>

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.075
<i> I start getting a rough shape.</i>

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:32.444
<i> But I have way too much steel.</i>

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:36.149
So I chop it off right there
and then forged my tip.

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.517
[Neilsen] Will's finally
putting a tip in his blade.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.620
Got a good amount
of material still to work with.

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:44.657
[Wil] And there we go.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.126
We've got Bobby quenching
over there on anvil number one.

00:03:47.726 --> 00:03:50.762
[Bobby]<i> Don't feel any tugs,
 cracks, tings.</i>

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:55.001
My blade's straight.
I'm very pleased at this point.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.435
[Justin]
<i> I go over to the grinder</i>

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:59.939
and I'm just trying to
"hog pall" this material off

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.640
so that I can get ready
for a quench.

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:04.577
I'm just praying
that I don't have a warp.

00:04:05.377 --> 00:04:06.779
-Justin quenched.
-Okay.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.782
[Justin]<i> I pull it out,
 it hardened, and I got a warp.</i>

00:04:12.451 --> 00:04:13.986
<i> I don't wanna snap this blade.</i>

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.922
<i> So I let it cool down
 a little bit in the vice.</i>

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:20.993
Warp's there but not as bad,
so I think I can grind it out.

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.263
[machine buzzing]

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:26.332
Will has quenched his blade.

00:04:27.299 --> 00:04:28.734
[Will]<i> And it's warped.</i>

00:04:29.401 --> 00:04:32.338
Try to flatten it out
but I'm afraid it's gonna break.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:35.408
So I heat it back up,
dunk it in the oil.

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:38.444
[judges] Whoa!

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:40.813
[shouts] Yo!
You want those eyebrows, kid?!

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:43.515
[Will] I grind as much as I can
and go straight into the edge,

00:04:43.582 --> 00:04:48.487
[Wil]
Five, four, three, two, one!

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:50.456
Blademiths, shut down
your machines, drop your tools,

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.391
Pull your blades out
of the acid.

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:55.427
This first round of competition
is over.

00:04:56.261 --> 00:04:58.564
Bladesmiths,
welcome to our strength test.

00:04:58.597 --> 00:05:01.200
The sheet metal stab and chop.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:05.271
I'm gonna take your weapons
and thrust and stab, chop, beat,

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:09.008
terrorize repeatedly into
these layers of sheet steel.

00:05:09.141 --> 00:05:10.476
It's gonna be fun.

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:13.145
Now what your blades do
to the steel,

00:05:13.211 --> 00:05:14.546
I'm not that concerned about.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.816
I wanna see what the steel
is gonna do to your blades.

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:19.185
And, Bobby, you're up first.

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:20.520
-You ready, bud?
-Yes, sir.

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:26.993
[grunting]

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:32.398
[grunting]

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.478
Pretty brutal. [exhales]

00:05:47.079 --> 00:05:48.180
All right, Bobby, good job.

00:05:48.246 --> 00:05:49.314
-You survived.
-Thank you.

00:05:49.381 --> 00:05:51.050
Tip penetrated nicely.

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:53.953
Went down
a little over half an inch.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.356
Edge held up just fine,
no problem.

00:05:56.923 --> 00:05:58.257
The handle...

00:05:58.424 --> 00:05:59.525
leaves a bit more
to be desired.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:02.128
-Yes, sir.
-It's a very lean guard here.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.830
Edges are kinda sharp so I was
definitely using a glove.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.399
-But it survived, so good job.
-Thank you.

00:06:07.432 --> 00:06:09.402
-How you feeling, Justin?
-Nervous.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:10.636
-[chuckles]
-Nervous? I'm not.

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:11.903
-Let's do it.
-All right.

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:14.374
[suspense music]

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:18.511
[grunting]

00:06:22.147 --> 00:06:23.383
[grunts]

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:28.388
[grunts]

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:34.794
[grunting]

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:48.541
Ow.

00:06:49.241 --> 00:06:51.576
My stomach drops.

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:54.680
There's a pinch point
or a hotspot on the handle

00:06:54.847 --> 00:06:55.815
and it's hurt him.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:03.989
Okay, this is one of the reasons
you wear the safety gear.

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:06.626
Justin, your pommel bit me.

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:09.895
And it didn't actually cut
a hole through the glove.

00:07:09.928 --> 00:07:12.631
It was sharp enough
to actually cut my skin

00:07:12.731 --> 00:07:13.966
through the fabric of the glove.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.234
But that being said,

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:17.269
I like the contouring
you did on it, though.

00:07:17.436 --> 00:07:19.371
Your edge got a couple spots

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:21.907
that had just a little bit
of glint to them.

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:24.176
Aside from that, you survived.
Good job.

00:07:24.276 --> 00:07:25.377
Thank you.

00:07:25.477 --> 00:07:27.045
Will, how you feeling?

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:29.214
[inhales] I'm optimistic.

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:30.650
It's a good way to be.
Let's see.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:31.851
Yes, sir.

00:07:33.018 --> 00:07:36.989
[grunting]

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:43.463
[grunts]

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:49.001
[grunts]

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:53.706
Cheer up, buddy. Good job.

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:55.440
You survived, Will. Good job.

00:07:55.574 --> 00:07:57.376
It's all I could hope for.

00:07:57.476 --> 00:08:00.213
A little bit of edge rolling
right here.

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:02.314
That's the biggest spot.
It's very small.

00:08:02.481 --> 00:08:03.715
-But it's there.
-Yes, sir.

00:08:03.882 --> 00:08:07.520
Biggest issue I had was
you got a warp in your blade.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:09.588
So those first couple strikes,

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:11.023
I was way off to the right.

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:12.458
But edge is still sharp.

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:15.228
-Everything's tight. Good job.
-Thank you, sir.

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:21.200
-Oh, my god.
-All right, bladesmiths.

00:08:21.266 --> 00:08:22.434
The strength test is complete.

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:23.869
Before we continue with testing,

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:26.739
I need just a moment to confer
with my colleagues.

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.342
The pommel was sharp enough.
Almost like a plow blade.

00:08:30.475 --> 00:08:31.744
I just pushed in,

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:34.180
it was able to break the skin
while wearing a glove.

00:08:36.382 --> 00:08:37.716
[tense music]

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.386
Justin, there's a big problem
with your blade.

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:42.587
<i> It hurt Jay
 while he was using it.</i>

00:08:42.721 --> 00:08:46.058
And a blade should never hurt
the end user.

00:08:47.126 --> 00:08:47.927
And for that reason,

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.995
you cannot move forward
with testing

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:52.298
and you cannot move forward
in this competition.

00:08:52.398 --> 00:08:53.866
I'd like to invite you
to shake my hand,

00:08:53.999 --> 00:08:56.735
shake your judges' hand,
shake your competitors' hand,

00:08:56.835 --> 00:08:58.337
and then please exit the forge.

00:08:58.404 --> 00:08:59.672
Come on, my friend.

00:09:00.306 --> 00:09:02.074
You did great.

00:09:02.174 --> 00:09:04.243
[indistinct whispers]

00:09:04.343 --> 00:09:05.577
[Justin]<i> Judges
 made the right call.</i>

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:07.345
<i> And I hope I get
 the opportunity to come back</i>

00:09:07.479 --> 00:09:08.814
<i> and try again.</i>

